  'Criminology',
  'Criminology examines the nature, causes, measurement, patterns, and prevention of crime in the United States. Students study major theoretical traditions, official and survey-based crime data, individual and social risk factors, inequality, social control, victimization, violent crime, property and white-collar crime, cybercrime, drugs, gangs, juvenile delinquency, policing, punishment, corrections, reentry, technology, and evidence-based prevention. The course emphasizes theory-data-policy integration and prepares students to evaluate crime claims with rigor and ethical care.',
  $crimjson${"slug": "criminology", "title": "Criminology", "description": "Criminology examines the nature, causes, measurement, patterns, and prevention of crime in the United States. Students study major theoretical traditions, official and survey-based crime data, individual and social risk factors, inequality, social control, victimization, violent crime, property and white-collar crime, cybercrime, drugs, gangs, juvenile delinquency, policing, punishment, corrections, reentry, technology, and evidence-based prevention. The course emphasizes theory-data-policy integration and prepares students to evaluate crime claims with rigor and ethical care.", "topics": [{"id": "3c8d76bb-29ec-48bf-8ee0-e15948e0709c", "type": "topic", "title": "Foundations of Criminology and the American Criminal Justice Context", "description": "This opening unit defines criminology as the study of crime, law, deviance, social harm, criminalization, and social response. Students learn how theory, data, institutions, and policy fit together.", "children": [{"id": "83df0fca-6674-4316-a6ed-d3f9e569ae3a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Crime, Deviance, and Social Harm", "children": [{"id": "c3ee7b4d-2dfa-475e-b57b-09a63c2486eb", "type": "concept", "title": "Definitions of crime"}, {"id": "0102ed5f-197d-4967-bd0b-f47126617252", "type": "concept", "title": "Criminalization"}, {"id": "606b3f67-f506-4bff-9e62-c115bbb08c12", "type": "concept", "title": "Moral panic and social reaction"}], "description": "The point is to distinguish legal crime from broader social harm and deviance."}, {"id": "18dc5113-2bb9-448d-bbcb-70b1dbc3a15f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Institutions and System Context", "children": [{"id": "1bfaff29-ac23-4e08-96b8-51b46d84e665", "type": "concept", "title": "Police, courts, corrections"}, {"id": "f5765c4b-b402-445e-8746-ce7ca6f79633", "type": "concept", "title": "Crime control and due process"}, {"id": "1e05eedd-ff55-4272-b650-883f61b9c067", "type": "concept", "title": "Community and state power"}], "description": "Students locate criminology within policing, courts, corrections, and communities."}, {"id": "c9b1ac39-44d4-4b57-8b0d-5d7b799a2809", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Criminological Imagination", "children": [{"id": "883ef984-06ab-49cb-9f1e-d77e546169f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Micro and macro levels"}, {"id": "aa7a2592-4464-424b-8295-c715b2e0074b", "type": "concept", "title": "Theory and evidence"}, {"id": "21e359f2-5237-4556-8a3d-41c4f4b5d454", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy consequences"}], "description": "This subtopic teaches students to connect individual cases to social structure."}]}, {"id": "71186626-bdf9-45e6-92ee-60b21a0791bc", "type": "topic", "title": "Measuring Crime: UCR/NIBRS, NCVS, Self-Report, and Data Ethics", "description": "Crime measurement shapes what society thinks crime is. Students learn the strengths, limits, and ethical risks of major U.S. crime-data systems.", "children": [{"id": "14a2d141-033e-4553-afef-09909584111b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Official Police Data", "children": [{"id": "7855ec38-8117-4b36-808e-622cd83cd051", "type": "concept", "title": "UCR and NIBRS"}, {"id": "8f912a48-55be-4d1e-875c-19ae0f1bb2a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Agency participation"}, {"id": "b5726e6f-8ffb-4643-888a-b30fa3862c11", "type": "concept", "title": "Clearance and reporting bias"}], "description": "Students learn what reported crime data capture and miss."}, {"id": "3ed30950-7889-4648-a170-8fba322dd009", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Victimization and Self-Report Data", "children": [{"id": "e40689d3-937e-4fbc-9840-e574f7f2fd6e", "type": "concept", "title": "NCVS"}, {"id": "4c3d9353-6ee8-49a8-bf16-b2d043a49150", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-report surveys"}, {"id": "69497b08-080a-489f-988d-d41e38be311e", "type": "concept", "title": "Underreporting and recall"}], "description": "The gist is to measure the dark figure of crime beyond police reports."}, {"id": "fdd717cc-b9cd-45a9-939d-bc95e63fc177", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data Ethics and Interpretation", "children": [{"id": "ab8905bc-d4a0-4e3d-a24e-ef8ac632ab3a", "type": "concept", "title": "Base rates"}, {"id": "f884de6b-446d-4bec-a90b-8fcf752daef0", "type": "concept", "title": "Racial and geographic bias"}, {"id": "8aeade6e-0e69-4e7e-9f63-873ef8d390e8", "type": "concept", "title": "Privacy and disclosure risks"}], "description": "Students learn to avoid simplistic claims from incomplete data."}]}, {"id": "87fa4bba-b41c-4f27-9c32-4f0baf621680", "type": "topic", "title": "Classical, Deterrence, Rational Choice, and Routine Activities Theories", "description": "This section studies crime as choice under constraints and opportunity. Students learn why punishment and prevention policy often begin with deterrence and opportunity.", "children": [{"id": "c248106a-68e2-4886-95c8-acdd157d5fe3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Classical School", "children": [{"id": "180df5e6-7cd4-42b3-b25f-7fb702345f86", "type": "concept", "title": "Beccaria"}, {"id": "4d890802-fe7d-47df-b6cf-f699a19b0f2f", "type": "concept", "title": "Bentham"}, {"id": "dc06b3ea-4952-4ca0-8036-71dd79b55c93", "type": "concept", "title": "Free will and punishment"}], "description": "Students examine the roots of legal rationality and proportional punishment."}, {"id": "082735fc-515f-47ff-880c-c6ecee5d69b2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Deterrence and Rational Choice", "children": [{"id": "ab0ad575-7e6b-4c87-8372-681724cfbed3", "type": "concept", "title": "General deterrence"}, {"id": "b67a7a50-f811-4429-b521-101125fdce2b", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific deterrence"}, {"id": "e0292a1c-ad9e-4ca1-ba19-08e7aef5b777", "type": "concept", "title": "Perceived risk"}], "description": "The point is to analyze how certainty, severity, and celerity affect behavior."}, {"id": "524b14b2-43fc-467f-b290-1683e0b8caea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Routine Activities and Opportunity", "children": [{"id": "a9a0526f-0060-4ad0-85ed-6c47c548aa9d", "type": "concept", "title": "Motivated offenders"}, {"id": "91545a77-91ae-4587-95f9-0d15cfe213f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Suitable targets"}, {"id": "5a5aa20f-c1ce-48be-80f2-aab337ddac43", "type": "concept", "title": "Capable guardianship"}], "description": "Students learn why crime clusters in places and routines."}]}, {"id": "5584c958-d5e1-4013-903e-91b94b650a5c", "type": "topic", "title": "Biological, Psychological, and Developmental Risk Factors", "description": "This unit covers individual-level risk without reducing crime to biology or pathology. Students learn how traits, trauma, cognition, and development interact with environment.", "children": [{"id": "50ed16ea-6ba8-4f6b-b084-385eb0b4c8d1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Biosocial Perspectives", "children": [{"id": "6a8c6eb5-d72f-4fdf-8976-b7482bd914ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Genetics and environment"}, {"id": "8bfae008-6052-4af5-ace6-2ae6377f1df2", "type": "concept", "title": "Neurodevelopment"}, {"id": "106ee293-1982-49eb-b127-99e178c07c9d", "type": "concept", "title": "Hormones and arousal"}], "description": "Students learn how biological risk is studied responsibly in social context."}, {"id": "708aad9e-ff9b-43c3-b07a-7f7b973400ae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Psychological Theories", "children": [{"id": "3cff70f9-8b36-4ed3-ba96-7da1fc4162a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Antisocial behavior"}, {"id": "bbda2d2f-9cf1-4d78-aa44-7897236597f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Aggression"}, {"id": "f811d10c-0bd9-4285-951d-a5506fc40e9f", "type": "concept", "title": "Trauma and disorders"}], "description": "The gist is to connect cognition, personality, learning, and mental health to offending."}, {"id": "e7942dcc-c6b0-4ea7-bfad-1de0f443b021", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Risk, Protection, and Ethics", "children": [{"id": "69b0d2a3-e4e7-424c-b323-53bf49a9e333", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk factors"}, {"id": "994a73b5-abd2-4fbd-b844-588f11456be3", "type": "concept", "title": "Protective factors"}, {"id": "0284a8d3-324a-4e5c-ab90-72583d92dfee", "type": "concept", "title": "Labeling and misuse"}], "description": "Students learn to distinguish explanation from prediction or stigma."}]}, {"id": "fa089167-4b1c-4a20-a43f-53c538849819", "type": "topic", "title": "Social Structure Theories: Strain, Anomie, Disorganization, and Inequality", "description": "Social structure theories explain crime through unequal opportunity, neighborhood conditions, and blocked goals. Students learn why place and inequality matter.", "children": [{"id": "64c62f52-3cd5-4d88-a62a-f1f496b0b495", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Strain and Anomie", "children": [{"id": "df4202ee-9fb7-4ec1-9753-4ee87422b15b", "type": "concept", "title": "Merton"}, {"id": "596f2035-a99d-4710-95b3-27cace03300f", "type": "concept", "title": "General strain"}, {"id": "5866884d-6b2a-4b82-a7be-f57246eb5f55", "type": "concept", "title": "Coping and anger"}], "description": "Students learn how blocked opportunity and pressure can generate crime."}, {"id": "19fa7abd-7f7f-4a4f-bc7b-3e80e9221ebd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social Disorganization", "children": [{"id": "a2f96ec1-bceb-462e-ae78-c5b07f7923f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Concentrated disadvantage"}, {"id": "ff3d2bd0-f6c0-4afd-b3b8-9754819a9db0", "type": "concept", "title": "Residential instability"}, {"id": "774ea11c-a6ce-46b1-a609-5829aa3be469", "type": "concept", "title": "Informal social control"}], "description": "The point is to understand neighborhood ecology and collective efficacy."}, {"id": "f7d6382a-cc77-4b57-99d3-dcd9a35cbb1c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inequality and Structural Violence", "children": [{"id": "bae4b050-fc0c-4949-b1af-683eb4a9432a", "type": "concept", "title": "Poverty and exclusion"}, {"id": "5f19e06b-8497-4c91-8e5e-bb745559facf", "type": "concept", "title": "Racial inequality"}, {"id": "bb354013-2795-4d15-83cd-22697248308a", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy feedback loops"}], "description": "Students connect crime to race, class, segregation, and institutional access."}]}, {"id": "8470b2b5-0aac-4cd8-9f80-3efcf9c8de84", "type": "topic", "title": "Social Process Theories: Learning, Control, Labeling, and Neutralization", "description": "Social process theories ask how people learn, justify, and desist from crime in interaction with others. Students focus on family, peers, schools, and identity.", "children": [{"id": "256913cb-869b-4185-ac8a-cffe86acac35", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Learning Theories", "children": [{"id": "8bc3b40d-5308-4923-be0e-318e7425d03d", "type": "concept", "title": "Differential association"}, {"id": "c1abea49-9d73-41c9-905d-62eb3ec5d7ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Social learning"}, {"id": "e4223f0b-3f59-4159-985b-f9ccaabe7733", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer networks"}], "description": "Students examine how crime is learned through groups and reinforcement."}, {"id": "59d032ee-7532-4fc7-80fc-6d14a49102a3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Control Theories", "children": [{"id": "a510f2a7-1e2b-4f58-a53f-a3216ce6c857", "type": "concept", "title": "Social bonds"}, {"id": "208631e6-e7e5-45ce-8b2b-5d4d5f221267", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-control"}, {"id": "36b99fd5-0cad-4a20-bba3-7d519c83efe8", "type": "concept", "title": "Informal controls"}], "description": "The gist is to study why most people conform most of the time."}, {"id": "99435bde-3824-4d09-a620-c23137a63f26", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Labeling and Neutralization", "children": [{"id": "3ce9eea7-def7-42b9-a0a7-e52cbc6e10bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Stigma"}, {"id": "cb7d251e-24a9-4027-b695-1972feafce7f", "type": "concept", "title": "Secondary deviance"}, {"id": "ec7f141a-e502-44fc-ae2e-e1f775f2a10f", "type": "concept", "title": "Techniques of neutralization"}], "description": "Students learn how justice-system reactions and excuses shape identity."}]}, {"id": "44e230c1-8a5e-4a05-8c46-d0965453eb96", "type": "topic", "title": "Critical, Conflict, Feminist, Queer, and Intersectional Criminology", "description": "This unit asks who defines crime and whose harms count. Students learn how power, inequality, and identity shape lawmaking and enforcement.", "children": [{"id": "84ebfe15-c094-4c80-82ee-a7e316ec6028", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Conflict and Critical Theory", "children": [{"id": "d234f304-e637-4508-98cb-420dd3661b33", "type": "concept", "title": "Class power"}, {"id": "ac887ac7-a337-4048-a575-57f1c77d1d49", "type": "concept", "title": "State violence"}, {"id": "3a5f50e8-a81b-4b51-b433-2e73c94709d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Criminalization of poverty"}], "description": "Students examine crime law as a product of power and social conflict."}, {"id": "93d65928-73bc-4abf-aa18-3ce2566b7998", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Feminist and Queer Criminology", "children": [{"id": "8242f0a0-536a-4b0b-9894-d8cb06545367", "type": "concept", "title": "Gendered violence"}, {"id": "1a5325bd-3923-4697-b41c-b52c1c4ab158", "type": "concept", "title": "Masculinities"}, {"id": "cae70174-48cf-404b-b91b-704a4d35d0b6", "type": "concept", "title": "LGBTQ criminalization"}], "description": "The point is to understand gender, sexuality, victimization, and criminalization."}, {"id": "ba5b344d-5703-48d2-8e68-ba43c93f5dc4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Intersectionality", "children": [{"id": "9b240c2c-e10a-4764-a088-6530ddd2defa", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiple marginalization"}, {"id": "73976162-144d-4a31-bc7a-a20e4e1e0cc5", "type": "concept", "title": "Cumulative disadvantage"}, {"id": "a1756e38-0a09-4eaf-8f56-3dc9b0326804", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy blind spots"}], "description": "Students analyze overlapping race, class, gender, age, immigration, and disability dynamics."}]}, {"id": "47b346e3-0044-403f-ba80-177681e585d6", "type": "topic", "title": "Life-Course, Developmental, and Integrated Theories", "description": "Life-course criminology explains onset, persistence, and desistance over time. Students learn why timing, turning points, and cumulative disadvantage matter.", "children": [{"id": "73f551a3-619d-400c-8f3a-a8a65fa858c1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Developmental Pathways", "children": [{"id": "2f8f66d1-6469-4bc3-9328-5ea71b124e3d", "type": "concept", "title": "Onset"}, {"id": "d4f5a04c-f991-427f-a956-fa6afd909e74", "type": "concept", "title": "Escalation"}, {"id": "7f50f744-8621-4f2c-90c3-eb8a2f2877c9", "type": "concept", "title": "Persistence"}], "description": "Students map how offending patterns unfold across age."}, {"id": "2bfcbde9-9a3a-426e-b912-ac8eec99d265", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Turning Points and Desistance", "children": [{"id": "006462a6-0326-4704-939b-8cff7f05c01c", "type": "concept", "title": "Employment"}, {"id": "43e3d735-dc89-4148-b1d1-f65e7dddc45d", "type": "concept", "title": "Marriage and family"}, {"id": "1091e187-5ca4-4f61-88d2-2a3c7f36f927", "type": "concept", "title": "Identity change"}], "description": "The gist is to explain why people stop offending."}, {"id": "d1d06df6-455d-4b72-908f-8fa59b7998c8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Integrated Theory", "children": [{"id": "d8540562-a3c6-46d2-85cd-e6f0c1425f54", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk-needs-responsivity"}, {"id": "ff91366d-2aa8-4450-b7e1-d34259e14f97", "type": "concept", "title": "Developmental ecology"}, {"id": "19098ad7-2170-4e10-8d52-a91689e1d5f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Multi-level explanation"}], "description": "Students learn when combining theories improves explanation."}]}, {"id": "bba5784e-5d8c-4203-8307-aa7433c0a684", "type": "topic", "title": "Victimology, Fear of Crime, Trauma, and Restorative Justice", "description": "Victimology centers harm, trauma, services, and victim rights. Students learn how victimization is patterned and how justice responses can help or harm.", "children": [{"id": "2bf8741f-443f-4a86-8b3c-b1b70659fff9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Victimization Patterns", "children": [{"id": "56f43a5b-62c2-4d30-a864-83af8ea4876d", "type": "concept", "title": "Repeat victimization"}, {"id": "ca730601-7aef-4a9d-939b-b3bf428f2e4f", "type": "concept", "title": "Victim-offender overlap"}, {"id": "0dddde3f-3954-49c1-971f-75b038dd7377", "type": "concept", "title": "Special populations"}], "description": "Students learn who is victimized, by whom, and under what conditions."}, {"id": "52cab52c-2c85-45bf-9143-2f270fda1563", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trauma and Secondary Victimization", "children": [{"id": "0d0c13aa-4755-412d-aa5c-be0ec7dbb48f", "type": "concept", "title": "PTSD and fear"}, {"id": "202d0815-4fd9-491b-bb3a-9c8ed40232bf", "type": "concept", "title": "System response"}, {"id": "81646f1d-342e-40fb-805e-ba4559904f9a", "type": "concept", "title": "Service gaps"}], "description": "The point is to understand impacts beyond the incident."}, {"id": "bdcdd87d-db18-4314-ba20-35a1518fc0ea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Restorative Justice", "children": [{"id": "8d58a71a-0f7e-4868-bcd2-e6c544a2f803", "type": "concept", "title": "Accountability"}, {"id": "2411cf44-0b05-4556-94ee-0455eed0e3e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Victim participation"}, {"id": "84fa15cf-5a07-42a0-8631-7b020cb40839", "type": "concept", "title": "Community healing"}], "description": "Students evaluate repair-focused approaches."}]}, {"id": "d138632d-c4b1-493f-97d6-d76b89bbe513", "type": "topic", "title": "Violent Crime: Homicide, Assault, Intimate Partner Violence, Sexual Violence, and Guns", "description": "This section studies serious interpersonal violence through data, theory, and prevention. Students learn to avoid one-size-fits-all explanations.", "children": [{"id": "0ee4e42b-3598-4c69-ad9d-705e6873a673", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Homicide and Assault", "children": [{"id": "080a83b2-8523-4479-bb77-19770c969f5c", "type": "concept", "title": "Weapon involvement"}, {"id": "a05eb1a1-fc7c-4308-a3bc-350cb4bb15fe", "type": "concept", "title": "Routine conflicts"}, {"id": "eef36d6a-3268-4cc2-90d0-85b585baa2a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Group violence"}], "description": "Students analyze patterns, situational dynamics, and disputes."}, {"id": "08b1fee7-27c6-440b-b4f3-4023f471c934", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gendered and Sexual Violence", "children": [{"id": "4c8f1f1f-e717-4ab4-b961-cd239eb5f08c", "type": "concept", "title": "IPV"}, {"id": "b77bbfa9-b285-4a44-aedd-ccbd76f07a8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Sexual assault"}, {"id": "35ff949b-e37c-41dd-a75e-d17408fe1ce5", "type": "concept", "title": "Victim blaming"}], "description": "The gist is to connect coercive control, trauma, and institutional response."}, {"id": "482c1f3b-5632-4af5-982e-ff6b57be888f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gun Violence Prevention", "children": [{"id": "78e7a6c9-3284-4977-9222-69e3fd012eb7", "type": "concept", "title": "Firearm access"}, {"id": "75a23cc3-9773-4ca6-a91f-89d75bfb37dd", "type": "concept", "title": "Hot spots"}, {"id": "0bfebf6b-edd1-4148-9426-c2fd3a11811c", "type": "concept", "title": "Community violence interruption"}], "description": "Students evaluate focused deterrence, place-based strategies, and legal limits."}]}, {"id": "ed889219-8906-4b08-8b36-767855ad8568", "type": "topic", "title": "Property, White-Collar, Corporate, Cyber, and Environmental Crime", "description": "Criminology must include hidden and high-harm crime beyond street offenses. Students compare conventional property crime with organizational and digital harms.", "children": [{"id": "5a949dcb-7a8a-4adc-9aee-1a1edca1f395", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Property Crime", "children": [{"id": "c88fd031-bb58-40c3-ae20-1f7d93bcadd2", "type": "concept", "title": "Target hardening"}, {"id": "72eeb8a8-4aea-468c-9b49-a93c5a0e08d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Repeat victimization"}, {"id": "5bf12ff3-6d55-4054-9faa-a8124da0336d", "type": "concept", "title": "Market demand"}], "description": "Students study theft, burglary, robbery, and routine opportunity."}, {"id": "339fff2c-b3bb-4a14-b2db-0fc2a8d34977", "type": "subtopic", "title": "White-Collar and Corporate Crime", "children": [{"id": "6df1d78c-dd23-4a91-a991-426ca559d098", "type": "concept", "title": "Fraud"}, {"id": "df926c84-3194-4db9-b9ce-f4b86547d276", "type": "concept", "title": "Regulatory violations"}, {"id": "a65a6798-1cd1-43ea-bd37-f99b8500a675", "type": "concept", "title": "Corporate accountability"}], "description": "The point is to understand harm produced through organizations and status."}, {"id": "db76f0ea-b2e0-4e55-b689-5beabbc42b0a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cyber and Environmental Crime", "children": [{"id": "6308c675-7ae4-4a24-9d77-5c7d0a36943c", "type": "concept", "title": "Identity theft"}, {"id": "2ae315f8-f7c5-40c3-954d-bd242c402ad9", "type": "concept", "title": "Ransomware"}, {"id": "ce1f756b-28ee-4a94-82ac-0f8f43fe1c04", "type": "concept", "title": "Pollution and environmental justice"}], "description": "Students examine technology-enabled and ecological harms."}]}, {"id": "3cedc50a-52ba-4356-a372-3bbc788487ef", "type": "topic", "title": "Drugs, Gangs, Organized Crime, and Illicit Markets", "description": "This unit studies illicit markets as social and economic systems. Students learn how enforcement, demand, supply, and community conditions interact.", "children": [{"id": "3fae96dc-c447-438c-9a82-dc03039f731c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Drug Use and Drug Markets", "children": [{"id": "f31db280-94c7-442e-b50a-69fc07883b27", "type": "concept", "title": "Harm reduction"}, {"id": "7687f411-05f7-4175-aa79-7de1bf17801b", "type": "concept", "title": "Prohibition effects"}, {"id": "db727fe8-1f9e-4d3f-a6d2-6a2e3d96326d", "type": "concept", "title": "Overdose context"}], "description": "Students distinguish drug use, dependence, distribution, and market violence."}, {"id": "0491dbb3-53be-43fc-aa53-124d085e89e9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gangs and Group Crime", "children": [{"id": "3ed7d26b-4473-450d-8182-77a06afc411f", "type": "concept", "title": "Group processes"}, {"id": "81a42a41-d7f3-41ef-9b3c-fc6a79ba8cd6", "type": "concept", "title": "Status and protection"}, {"id": "0f5c42d2-d14f-4c4b-bfe6-615161209225", "type": "concept", "title": "Violence contagion"}], "description": "The gist is to understand gangs as social networks, identity, and neighborhood phenomena."}, {"id": "586e153b-8c84-4d8c-a2d5-34bd3f24b8e1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Organized Crime and Trafficking", "children": [{"id": "3e3dd8fc-5f81-42c7-9def-c9c179edb00c", "type": "concept", "title": "Enterprise structure"}, {"id": "305962b8-be2d-4c05-a80d-b5661eab32f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Corruption"}, {"id": "072e6116-e622-4687-a093-0c295d51c1f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Transnational markets"}], "description": "Students analyze networked illicit enterprise."}]}, {"id": "486174ca-a874-4271-b400-c92c6068e5c6", "type": "topic", "title": "Juvenile Delinquency, Schools, Families, and Community Interventions", "description": "Youth offending is central to criminological theory and policy. Students learn how development, schools, families, and communities shape delinquency and intervention.", "children": [{"id": "a323c2ba-3b75-4b89-9c81-ed1063c79348", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Youth Development", "children": [{"id": "bec63160-42f3-4d17-8995-56c0abedf2a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Brain development"}, {"id": "9b00e839-b5fc-4034-9ac7-64b23deef4a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Peer influence"}, {"id": "137965e1-7b67-4bfd-a0f2-236f547b7a63", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk-taking"}], "description": "Students connect adolescent development to offending and desistance."}, {"id": "334e4d7d-6f7d-4fc0-b2e9-ca778b32c7e7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Schools and Families", "children": [{"id": "a1581801-cbb2-4c15-b14b-732f0209bf9e", "type": "concept", "title": "School discipline"}, {"id": "f8c09165-5733-47c4-8bea-d7e482fd372a", "type": "concept", "title": "Family stress"}, {"id": "f3618b0b-9aea-44e2-baab-ff98527c4462", "type": "concept", "title": "School-to-prison pipeline"}], "description": "The point is to study institutions that can protect or punish."}, {"id": "4e543d0f-742b-415c-949c-90d2bf2b5164", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interventions", "children": [{"id": "559e23c8-998d-4bcf-8355-c07f9c9340a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Diversion"}, {"id": "ee1e04ee-938b-4e8f-a703-a18381667ecb", "type": "concept", "title": "MST and family models"}, {"id": "24120ca5-e87b-48f9-bea3-0a4e7e5c7906", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence ratings"}], "description": "Students evaluate diversion, mentoring, family therapy, and community programs."}]}, {"id": "8a69aa98-d7b5-4dea-8a03-e106896cc245", "type": "topic", "title": "Punishment, Policing, Corrections, Reentry, and Mass Incarceration", "description": "This section asks how society responds to crime and with what consequences. Students connect theory to policing, sentencing, prisons, community corrections, and reentry.", "children": [{"id": "abd6b717-b42e-45de-959e-01f0f0533c13", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policing and Legitimacy", "children": [{"id": "6ffb21f6-bb9d-4b6c-a76f-300a85c1da10", "type": "concept", "title": "Hot spots policing"}, {"id": "576cbf18-8106-468d-b5ee-1f55114acc19", "type": "concept", "title": "Procedural justice"}, {"id": "1c4ca2cd-ef8d-471d-aced-d362142c1943", "type": "concept", "title": "Accountability"}], "description": "Students evaluate strategies and community trust."}, {"id": "e3b91ba8-b014-4e5d-9077-6df9179d21f1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Punishment and Corrections", "children": [{"id": "c515902e-d649-4d55-ae54-2dbe298db88c", "type": "concept", "title": "Sentencing"}, {"id": "96a44056-1390-42e1-a4d2-26eb7ed79030", "type": "concept", "title": "Prisons and jails"}, {"id": "e299371b-74e0-499e-b44a-5457e0c5ec00", "type": "concept", "title": "Probation and parole"}], "description": "The gist is to compare deterrence, incapacitation, retribution, rehabilitation, and restorative aims."}, {"id": "5732ddca-0093-46bb-8225-0c1e2baeb4fb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reentry and Recidivism", "children": [{"